A||||10||AkursedX||Do 88's have same carpet color?||||5||
Z||000000||AkursedX||03-18-2001||07:30 PM||||I was wondering if someone could tell me if the carpet colors for the '88 "beechwood" interior is the same as the 84-87 "tan" color? <P>Thanks in advance  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||03-18-2001||07:58 PM||||They are different......beechwood is an '88 only color. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||03-19-2001||02:59 PM||||all of the trim pieces in an '88 are a darker tan called "Beechwood" except the carpet and the lower carpet on the door panels........that is the same as the carpet used for the "Buckskin" tan on the other model years........||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||03-19-2001||03:08 PM||||I beg to differ......nothing in an '88 beechwood interior is shared with any other year Fiero.  The carpets are a different shade, as are the trim panels.  I have owned numerous '88s with beechwood interiors (including my 16K mile GT), so I am certain.||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||03-19-2001||03:25 PM||||ok Mike, we have a difference of opinion I guess -- I just walked down into the shop and looked at three Beechwood '88's and then two '87s (one of them mine) and an '86 with the Buckskin interior and all of the carpets are the very same color........those must be the California versions........||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieroparts.com||03-19-2001||05:44 PM||||Well.. I have been selling Fiero parts for over 12 years the <BR>84-85 is dark brown<BR>86-87 is dark saddle   20681853<BR>88 med. beechwood      10080090<P><BR>I have a brand NEW set of mats, one of each color, and THEY ARE NOT THE SAME COLOR!||||reg||11
Z||000006||qwikgta||03-19-2001||09:43 PM||||Since we are on the subject, does ACC (or anyone else) sell the correct 88 "Beachwood" carpet.  If not, were do we get the original type of carpet.  <P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||5
Z||000007||stimpy||03-19-2001||10:43 PM||||Ouch! Let's not let this get too ugly. Why we wanna know is that I am making a sub-box for Joe (aKursedX) and want to know if I need to find an 88 to scavenge or if it would make a huge diff if I used pre-88 carpet to cover it.  This is not a concours restoration question, and if it looks the same to Terry, I can get the conclusion that it's close enough. Thanks for the help fellas.||||reg||1
Z||000008||AkursedX||03-19-2001||11:26 PM||||Hmmm, it seems me and Stimpy have begun somewhat of a controversey here.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>But even if they are different colors, it isn't that much of a difference where it'll really affect the look of my sub-box anyways  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000009||Black88GT||03-19-2001||11:43 PM||||Beechwood is different for sure.  I compared it to see if it was so.  I might just use headliner fabric for the cover on my sub box because I don't have the guts to cut up some stock beechwood carpeting.<P>Oh yeah forgot to mention, Mike is the expert on Beechwood interior stuff, so I would take his word for it alone.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp">  <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 03-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||fieroshop||03-20-2001||01:21 PM||||Everybody is right and at the same time wrong.<BR>The 88 beechwood carpet is the same in color even though it has a different part number.<BR>The difference id that 87 back have a felt like underlayment while the 88 has a foam pad glued to the carpet.<BR>I know this for the reason that I have had to restore several fieros at our shop. So guys quit the argument, it is petty.<BR>*7 and 88 grey is also a different part number for the same reason. <P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
